  "instructions": {
    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "3a3d1a64c20ad9cd0448e301d04f5933",
        "content": [
          "You answer questions about Databricks cost and the DPO optimisation backlog. All money is in USD.\n",
          "Data covers a rolling 30-day window; monthly_cost is the window cost scaled to 30 days.\n",
          "Scoring: score = 0.35*V + 0.25*C + 0.20*F + 0.20*R (V value, C confidence, F feasibility, R reversibility,\n",
          "each 0-1). Priority: P1 if score >= 0.75, P2 if >= 0.60, else P3. Order backlogs by score DESC, finding_id.\n",
          "est_monthly_savings is a hypothesis until a benchmark validates it: always call it \"estimated\" and never\n",
          "add it up as guaranteed savings. status NEEDS_REVIEW means nobody has validated the finding yet.\n",
          "workload_key is '<type>:<id>', e.g. 'job:123', 'cluster:abc', 'query:<fingerprint>', 'warehouse:<id>'.\n",
          "A NULL cost_center is untagged spend: show it as '(untagged)'.\n",
          "Rule ids R01-R17 (rule_id like 'R01_COMPUTE_IDLE'): R01 idle all-purpose cluster, R02 oversized job\n",
          "cluster, R03 auto-termination, R04 old runtime, R05 job on all-purpose compute, R06 job failure rate,\n",
          "R07 task skew, R08 runtime regression, R09 daily cost spike, R10 untagged spend, R11 no file pruning,\n",
          "R12 spill, R13 repeated query without cache, R14 warehouse queuing, R15 small files, R16 SQL anti-pattern,\n",
          "R17 plain file copy that could move to native cloud copy tools.\n",
          "Budget outlook (budget_outlook, one row per cost centre for the current month): actual_mtd is spend so\n",
          "far this month, forecast_remaining the forecast for the rest of the month, projected_total = actual_mtd +\n",
          "forecast_remaining, projected_lower/projected_upper the prediction interval. status: OVER_BUDGET (already\n",
          "above budget), AT_RISK (projection above budget), WATCH (only the upper bound is above), ON_TRACK, NO_BUDGET\n",
          "(no budget set). method says how the forecast was made: ai_forecast (Databricks AI forecasting) or baseline\n",
          "(weekday average). cost_forecast holds the daily forecast with lower and upper bounds. Forecasts are\n",
          "estimates: always give the range, not just the point value.\n",
          "Never write INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, MERGE, CREATE, DROP, GRANT or any other statement that changes data\n",
          "or access. Answer with SELECT queries only.\n",
          "Tables: recommendations = scored backlog (one row per finding); recommendation_narratives = plain-language\n",
          "explanation per finding (join on finding_id); workload_summary = cost per workload; job_scorecard = job\n",
          "reliability and cost; cost_by_dimension = daily cost by product, SKU, workspace, cost centre and run_as.\n",
          "These are secured views: each person sees only the cost centres they are mapped to. For some people\n",
          "share_of_total, cost_rank, rank, savings_rank and evidence are NULL by design and run_as is a hashed id.\n",
          "When asked for a share or a rank, compute it over the visible rows (e.g. with a window function) and say\n",
          "it is \"of the spend you can see\". Never try to work out account-wide totals, other cost centres or real\n",
          "identities, and do not explain how the masking works beyond saying some values are restricted."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "example_question_sqls": [
      {
        "id": "30f0e9f9b5c84ef05103b17ce4d2d232",
        "question": [
          "Which workloads cost the most per month, with their share of visible spend?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT workload_key, workload_type, coalesce(cost_center, '(untagged)') AS cost_center,\n",
          "       round(monthly_cost, 2) AS monthly_cost,\n",
          "       round(monthly_cost / nullif(sum(monthly_cost) OVER (), 0) * 100, 1) AS share_of_visible_pct\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.workload_summary\n",
          "ORDER BY monthly_cost DESC\n",
          "LIMIT 10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "344b7d20754bf892caedcdfdd33b6a2f",
        "question": [
          "What did each cost centre spend in the window?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT coalesce(cost_center, '(untagged)') AS cost_center, round(sum(cost), 2) AS cost,\n",
          "       round(sum(dbus), 1) AS dbus\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.cost_by_dimension\n",
          "GROUP BY 1\n",
          "ORDER BY cost DESC"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "41b79d4452d2116c5a4110f3e01bf6ee",
        "question": [
          "Which jobs fail most often?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT job_name, runs, failed, round(failure_rate * 100, 1) AS failure_pct,\n",
          "       round(monthly_cost, 2) AS monthly_cost, round(cost_per_success, 2) AS cost_per_success\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.job_scorecard\n",
          "WHERE runs > 0\n",
          "ORDER BY failure_rate DESC, monthly_cost DESC\n",
          "LIMIT 10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "44071f9db1e1400fafeec4fe236d3d7a",
        "question": [
          "Which cost centres are at risk of going over budget this month?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT cost_center, status, round(budget, 2) AS budget, round(actual_mtd, 2) AS spent_so_far,\n",
          "       round(projected_total, 2) AS projected_month_total,\n",
          "       round(projected_lower, 2) AS projected_low, round(projected_upper, 2) AS projected_high,\n",
          "       round(pct_of_budget * 100, 1) AS pct_of_budget, days_remaining, method\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.budget_outlook\n",
          "ORDER BY CASE status WHEN 'OVER_BUDGET' THEN 1 WHEN 'AT_RISK' THEN 2 WHEN 'WATCH' THEN 3\n",
          "                     WHEN 'ON_TRACK' THEN 4 ELSE 5 END, pct_of_budget DESC"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "7fa6c9dbd1cfc110c546bf816513caf0",
        "question": [
          "What is the estimated monthly saving per category and priority?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT category, priority, count(*) AS findings,\n",
          "       round(sum(coalesce(est_monthly_savings, 0)), 2) AS estimated_monthly_savings\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.recommendations\n",
          "GROUP BY category, priority\n",
          "ORDER BY estimated_monthly_savings DESC"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "a1245078a480ee8e21b80d383fa576b2",
        "question": [
          "Show daily cost by product"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT usage_date, billing_origin_product AS product, round(sum(cost), 2) AS cost\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.cost_by_dimension\n",
          "GROUP BY usage_date, billing_origin_product\n",
          "ORDER BY usage_date, product"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "b03c4dc5161d527a440632c9b9a96f7e",
        "question": [
          "What are the top 10 recommendations by score?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT rec.priority, round(rec.score, 3) AS score, rec.rule_id, rec.title, rec.workload_key,\n",
          "       coalesce(rec.cost_center, '(untagged)') AS cost_center,\n",
          "       round(rec.est_monthly_savings, 2) AS estimated_monthly_savings, rec.action, n.narrative\n",
          "FROM workspace.dpo_reporting.recommendations rec\n",
          "LEFT JOIN workspace.dpo_reporting.recommendation_narratives n ON n.finding_id = rec.finding_id\n",
          "ORDER BY rec.score DESC, rec.finding_id\n",
          "LIMIT 10"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "sql_snippets": {
      "measures": [
        {
          "id": "3aac73626b6605e237a1a27eb648d8c1",
          "alias": "p1_findings",
          "display_name": "P1 findings",
          "sql": [
            "COUNT_IF(recommendations.priority = 'P1')"
